<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kintyre</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kintyre is a long peninsula in the south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, whose southern tip, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mull-of-kintyre">Mull of Kintyre</a>, lies about 20 kilometres from Ireland. It was the heartland of the Cenél nGabráin, one of the ruling kindreds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, and later part of the Kingdom of the Isles and the Lordship of the Isles.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kintyre.jpg" alt="Kintyre" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Ferguson · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johnston%27s_Point_Feochaig_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4699157.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
